13:T640,With global defense budgets on the rise and escalating geopolitical tensions driving heightened demand for advanced military technologies, defense stocks and exchange-traded funds (ETFs) have captured growing interest from investors seeking both stability and growth potential in the sector.  Defense ETFs provide a diversified avenue for gaining exposure to a broad range of companies involved in aerospace, cybersecurity, weapons systems, defense contracting, and related technologies, allowing investors to participate in the overall growth of the defense industry while mitigating company-specific risks.  These funds often include established industry giants with longstanding government contracts and proven operational track records, as well as emerging players innovating in areas such as autonomous systems, missile defense, cybersecurity solutions, and unmanned aerial vehicles, thereby offering a balance between stability and growth potential.  Analysts emphasize that defense investments can benefit significantly from rising government expenditure, as increased funding for military programs often translates into expanded contracts, research and development budgets, and long-term revenue streams for companies operating in the sector.  Government procurement policies, budget allocations, and multi-year defense programs create a relatively predictable demand environment, which can provide resilience against broader market volatility and cyclical economic fluctuations.  At the same time, investors are advised to remain attentive to key risk factors inherent in the defense sector.4:[["$","$Lf",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/investing/best-defense-etfs-2025/\"},\"headline\":\"Best Defense ETFs to Watch in 2025\",\"description\":\"As global military spending rises, these defense-focus